          "id": "claim-8ef30e9e100101a18cf2",
          "sourceIds": [
            "places-722b268c12cec9e1cb51",
            "places-7fb8137cf82d592b243e"
          ],
          "text": "ExecuteAsync creates a producer and repeatedly calls PublishPending until cancellation, logging other exceptions as PUBLISH_RETRY and waiting one second between attempts. Each publish opens a database transaction and selects one eligible unpublished row in created_at order with FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED; no row returns without sending. Otherwise it extracts the place ID from the payload, awaits a keyed send to weather.place-requested, marks the row published, and commits. A broker send followed by a transaction failure or crash can leave the row eligible for replay. The Dashboard and Forecasts topic mappings are agent-proposed; subscription, downstream processing and hosted-service activation remain unverified."
        },
        "title": "Publish pending place requests"
      }
    ],
